   "lessons": [
    "A chat model answers with prose THEN a fenced block. An extractor that only strips a leading fence feeds the prose to exec() and rejects every sample - measured as p=0.000 on a model that solves the task at p=0.062.",
    "vLLM /v1/completions applies no chat template; instruct models degrade badly through it and small models worst.",
    "rocm-smi --showpids reports KFD handles, not OS pids - kill -9 against those numbers hits nothing while the real process holds 44 GB.",
    "vLLM renames its worker to VLLM::EngineCore, so pkill -f vllm never matches it.",
    "A kill pattern embedded in the command that runs it matches its own command line. Put the pattern in a file, or bracket-escape it."
   ],
   "ts": "20260805T203004Z"
  },
